{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_tracer_api", "label": "Tracer API", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_tracer", "label": "Tracer interface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "startSpan, withActiveSpan, activeSpan, injectContext and extractContext - a minimal surface close to the OpenTelemetry API but smaller, with no SDK dependency since you bring your own."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_span", "label": "Span interface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "context, setAttribute, setStatus, recordException, end, and a readonly ended flag; after end further methods are no-ops."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_spanoptions", "label": "SpanOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "parent (undefined uses the active span, null forces a root), initial attributes, kind and a start-time override."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_nooptracer", "label": "NoopTracer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The default: tracing disabled, every call short-circuited."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_withactivespan", "label": "withActiveSpan", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs a callback with a span active so child spans auto-link as children; it uses AsyncLocalStorage under the hood, so the active span propagates across awaits."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_injectcontext", "label": "injectContext and extractContext", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The cross-wire pair - the cluster transport puts carriers into wire envelopes automatically, and outside the actor system you inject and extract manually to bridge tracing across services."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_tracecarrier", "label": "TraceCarrier", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A key-value map, W3C-compatible so spans serialize to traceparent for downstream OTel services."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_tracing_off_costs_a_field_read", "label": "Tracing off costs a field read", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Since the message path resolves the tracer from a plain field on the ActorSystem rather than through the extension registry, an untraced message allocates nothing and makes no async-storage lookup on its account. This used to be documented as zero-cost and that was not true: the receive path resolved the tracing extension twice per message and the send path once more, each a map lookup plus two calls, on every message whether or not anything was tracing. The claim is now accurate rather than aspirational - a field read and a null check, not nothing."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_span_lifetime", "label": "Span lifetime", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Spans must be ended or the tracer leaks memory and the span never exports. The framework auto-ends the spans it creates for message handling; user code owns the ones it creates, and try/finally is the pattern."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_span_attributes_pii", "label": "Span attributes and PII", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Traces are typically less-protected than primary databases, so personal data, secrets and anything privacy-sensitive do not belong in attributes."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_pipeto_span_gap_tracer_api", "label": "pipeTo does not propagate the active span (Tracer API)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The target handler runs in a fresh scope, so capture the carrier before piping."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_tracer_api", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_tracer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_tracer_api", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_span", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_tracer_api", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_spanoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_tracer_api", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_nooptracer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_tracer_api", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_withactivespan", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_tracer_api", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_tracer_api_injectcontext", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/tracer-api.mdx", 